{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. The scheduler was running—the job had six runs—but two bugs caused complete silence:\n\n- Missing `USER` in the launchd environment caused `claude` to fail with “Not logged in.” Added `USER=vk` in `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist:27`.\n- `status=$?` terminated the zsh script because `status` is read-only, preventing failure notifications. Renamed it to `rc` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh:19`.\n\nFull evidence and applicable parts of the colleague’s note are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nVerified with syntax/plist checks and end-to-end runs using local agent/notifier stand-ins. Both success and forced-failure notifications worked; no external services were contacted. The modified plist still needs reloading in the real home directory."}
